Read CLAUDE.md.

Implement Sprint 0.2: Apache Kafka (KRaft, single broker) and the
transactional outbox pattern.

Deliver:

- migrations/000002_outbox.up.sql — `outbox` table:
  id uuid PK, tenant_id uuid NOT NULL, topic text NOT NULL, key text,
  payload jsonb NOT NULL, headers jsonb, created_at timestamptz,
  dispatched_at timestamptz NULL, attempts int DEFAULT 0,
  last_error text. Index on (dispatched_at, created_at) WHERE dispatched_at
  IS NULL. ENABLE + FORCE RLS. Policy uses current_tenant(). app_user gets
  SELECT, INSERT. app_user gets UPDATE only on dispatched_at, attempts,
  last_error (relay uses these).

- internal/outbox/writer.go — `Append(ctx, tx, topic, key, payload)`
  inserts into outbox within the caller's transaction. Returns
  ErrNoTenant if context has no tenant. No direct Kafka call from
  handlers, ever.

- internal/outbox/relay.go — reads undispatched outbox rows in batches,
  publishes via Kafka transactional producer, marks dispatched in the
  same tx that the row was read. Producer is idempotent
  (enable.idempotence=true, transactional.id per worker instance).
  On publish failure: increment attempts, record last_error, leave
  dispatched_at NULL, retry with exponential backoff up to 10 attempts.
  After 10: log to stderr and stop retrying (ops will investigate).

- cmd/relay/main.go — runs the relay worker. Connect as a dedicated
  `relay_user` role (new: SELECT on outbox, UPDATE on
  dispatched_at/attempts/last_error only). Fails closed if it cannot
  reach Kafka.

- internal/account/repository.go — modify Create to also call
  outbox.Append(ctx, tx, "ratify.account.created", accountID, payload)
  in the same transaction as the insert. The event must be published iff
  the account is committed.

- deploy/docker-compose.yml — add kafka (apache/kafka:4.0.0, KRaft,
  RF=1, KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=-Xms512m -Xmx1024m, mem_limit 2g, cpus 1.0,
  controller+boker role, advertised listener kafka:9092) and relay (new
  service, mem_limit 512m, cpus 0.25, depends_on kafka healthy and
  postgres healthy and migrate completed).

- deploy/initdb/01-roles.sql — add relay_user role with the grants above.

- tests/outbox_test.go — three subtests:
  1. Account creation writes exactly one outbox row in the same tx
     (rollback test: force a failure after Append, confirm no account
     AND no outbox row).
  2. Relay publishes the row to Kafka and marks dispatched_at within
     2 seconds of commit.
  3. Relay crash mid-publish (kill the relay process between read and
     mark-dispatched) does NOT produce a duplicate Kafka message on
     restart, because the producer is idempotent and the tx is not
     committed. Verify consumer sees exactly one message.

- Update Makefile: `make test` runs both isolation and outbox tests.

Acceptance criteria:
